==============================================================================
6. Demo lectures (served by the live site; not in this repository)
==============================================================================

Four talks from Electromagnetic Field 2026, recorded by the EMF Video Team and C3VOC, published on media.ccc.de under
the Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International licence (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/):

- "You Are Part Virus: How Biological Viruses Hack Cells", Christopher Binny
  https://media.ccc.de/v/emf2026-149-1-you-are-part-virus-how-biological-viruses-hack-cells
- "Data Visualisation: The Good, The Bad, The Ugly and the Beautiful", Charlotte Rutherford
  https://media.ccc.de/v/emf2026-241-1-data-visualisation-the-good-the-bad-the-ugly
- "It's the End of RSA as We Know It (And I Feel Fine): An Introduction to Post-Quantum Cryptography", Lucy Bell
  https://media.ccc.de/v/emf2026-242-1-its-the-end-of-rsa-as-we-know-it-and-i-feel-fine
- "A Brief History of the QR Code, and other scannable things", Jon Ginn
  https://media.ccc.de/v/emf2026-234-1-a-brief-history-of-the-qr-code-and-other-scannable-things

Changes: trimmed (title card, sponsor logos, jingle and closing licence card cut; two talks end at a section break),
re-encoded for streaming (720p H.264, mono Opus), and AI tracks added (captions, translations, slide descriptions,
chapters, glossary, recap) by this project's agents with Meta models. The trimmed videos and the derived tracks are
shared under CC BY-SA 4.0. The cuts are in deploy/media/demo-lectures.sh.

==============================================================================
7. Stills from the demo lectures (web/public/talks/)
==============================================================================

Eight frames of the four demo lectures in section 6, two per talk, cut from the trimmed 720p recordings, cropped to
16:9 and saved as WebP (480 px, and up to 960 px wide). They are adaptations of those CC BY-SA 4.0 works and are
shared under CC BY-SA 4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/). Credit: the talk's speaker,
Electromagnetic Field 2026, recorded by the EMF Video Team and C3VOC. The hub shows each still's credit next to it.
Slides whose main content is a photograph or someone else's figure were left out (ticket 0001, decision 0036);
these show the speakers' own slides or the speakers themselves.

- virus.webp: slide 14, "Alternate Reading Frames", at 12:24 of the cut; Christopher Binny
- virus-rec.webp: a slide of a viral genome map, at 10:00; Christopher Binny
- dataviz.webp: Charlotte Rutherford speaking by video link, at 1:42; Charlotte Rutherford
- dataviz-rec.webp: slide "Rule (of thumb) 2: The Visual Variable Matters", at 7:12; Charlotte Rutherford
- rsa.webp: slide "Classical Public Key Encryption", at 13:12; Lucy Bell
- rsa-rec.webp: slide "Fundamentals of Quantum Mechanics", at 10:24; Lucy Bell
- qrcode.webp: Jon Ginn on stage, at 0:24; Jon Ginn
- qrcode-rec.webp: the stage and audience, at 0:02; Jon Ginn
